; Evaluate the complete relation of Conditional absent-member findings. Each
; finding names a class that certainly reaches the access and certainly lacks
; the member. Other unclassified values may also reach it. A listed global dynamic
; write is allowed only when every matching write has no receiver bound and an
; Any member-name set. A DeclaredParameter origin is allowed only for one
; annotated workspace class with no workspace subclasses, unresolved or
; unmodeled external bases, or dynamic-attribute hooks; the condition states
; that it is as annotated and no workspace subclass of that class exists.
; Proven findings belong to bifrost.correctness.python-absent-member.
(policy
  :schema-version 1
  :id "bifrost.correctness.python-absent-member-conditional"
  :name "Python absent member (conditional)"
  :message "this Python access may lack the member under the receiver and remainder conditions stated in the finding"
  :severity warning
  :description "Caller-driven class-set propagation proves that a class reaches this access and lacks the accessed member, but other unclassified receiver values may also reach the access. A global dynamic write may remain as a conditional remainder only when every matching write has no receiver bound and an Any member-name set; the finding condition names the write sites that could install the member. A DeclaredParameter origin is admitted only when its annotation resolves to exactly one workspace class and the existing surface checks establish no workspace subclasses, unresolved or unmodeled external bases, or dynamic-attribute hooks. Its condition states that the receiver has the annotated type and no workspace subclass of that class exists. A remainder that can mean the class should have been filtered on this path, such as an unmodeled guard or predicate, or an incomplete or budget-limited solve, suppresses the finding. Guard-only class membership, uncertain flow into the class, open member models, and bounded or member-attributed writes that could install the member also suppress it. Missing Python declaration-model coverage makes the run inconclusive."
  :help-uri "https://bifrost.brokk.ai/static-analysis-policies/#built-in-code-smell-pack"
  :tags ["correctness" "python" "type-flow"]
  :analysis (analysis
    :type assertion
    (bind :name finding
      :query (rql :schema-version 1
        (language python
          (absent-member :proof conditional
            (procedure-of
              (callable))))))
    (group :name by-access-class :by (finding.id)
      (aggregate :name violations :op count))
    (assert :group by-access-class :value violations :cardinality (exactly 0))))
